## 4. Self-hosting / VibeCodeWorker license; paid only

Running VibeCodeWorker or any material part of the Covered Work on your
own infrastructure ("self-hosting") requires a current paid
VibeCodeWorker Self-Hosted plan. There is no free, trial, or implied
self-host right.

- **Mid-tier (standard self-host): $420/month per organization.**
  Includes up to 100 user seats under the org. Additional seats:
  **$4.20/month per seat.** Plan includes permission to self-host plus
  help with self-hosting, workspaces, orchestration, messaging, and
  support. Metered API / compute used through our orchestration carries
  a **15% markup** over at-cost provider bills.
- **Enterprise / hyperscaler: custom quote - Talk to Sales.**
  Volume pricing available down to as little as a **9% API / compute
  markup**, depending on scale, term, prepayment, and support scope.
  Contact matt@mattyjacks.com for a written quote. No enterprise rights
  exist until a signed order or written quote is in place.

Seats are counted per named user with access during the billing period,
including bots operated on a user's behalf where applicable per your
order. Exceeding your seat count is billed as additional seats. Current
prices and plan details live at https://4weird.com/pricing.

## 5. Platform fee - 25% cut is part of every price

Every hosted price is gross and already includes our platform service
fee (standard: **25% platform / 75% provider or creator as on-site
platform credits**), never added
on top. Coins (100 coins = $1.00), game rentals, agent rentals, team
compute, game AI, support/tips, and campaign contributions all settle on
this basis, as metered and attributed server-side. Coins are spendable
on cloud computing, game credits, and other on-site services only;
never cash-out, never withdrawable. Circumventing,
obscuring, or routing around metering or the platform fee; including
off-platform settlement to avoid it; violates this license and the
Terms and may result in suspension, forfeiture of credits, and billing
for amounts owed.

## 6. Contributions; automatic assignment to us

By submitting, uploading, posting, or otherwise making available any
game, code, art, audio, video, text, feedback, bug report, or other
work on or through the platform or this repo (a "Contribution"), you
agree:

1. You presently assign to MattyJacks LLC all right, title, and
   interest in the Contribution, worldwide, including copyrights and
   all other intellectual-property rights, to the fullest extent
   permitted by law;
2. To the extent any rights cannot be assigned, you grant us an
   exclusive, irrevocable, perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free,
   transferable, sublicensable license to use them in any manner;
3. You waive moral rights / attribution rights to the extent waivable,
   and agree not to assert them against us or our licensees;
4. You represent you have the authority to grant the above and that the
   Contribution does not infringe third-party rights.

Effect: contributors do not retain ownership of work contributed through
the platform. We may use, improve, modify, adapt, combine, distribute,
commercialize, or discontinue Contributions without further permission,
notice, or compensation, except where the Terms expressly provide
creator coin credits (e.g. the 75% creator share of on-site platform
credits on included-price transactions; spendable on cloud computing,
game credits, and other on-site services only, never cash-out). Prior versions of a Contribution already assigned remain
assigned even if you later delete your account.

## 7. We may improve and modify games without creator permission

We reserve the right to fix, patch, optimize, re-balance, moderate,
re-package, re-render, translate, port, or otherwise modify any game or
Contribution on the Service; including via VibeCodeWorker QA loops,
human review, or automated tooling; without seeking the creator's
prior permission. We may also remove or suspend games for safety, legal,
quality, or operational reasons. Gameplay telemetry, QA findings, and
derived fixes may be used across the platform.

## 8. Attribution; credit VibeCodeWorker in your game

If you used VibeCodeWorker to help build, test, or improve your game,
you must include a visible credit in the game's credits (and, where the
game has one, its about/readme screen) substantially in this form:

> "Built with help from 4weird VibeCodeWorker; https://4weird.com/vibecodeworker"

Removal or obscuring of a required credit is a license violation. We may
request cure within 14 days; uncured or repeated violations may result
in delisting and termination of related distribution rights.

## 9. Payment; prepay preferred; amounts owed are enforceable

We prefer prepayment. Fees are due as stated on https://4weird.com/pricing,
your order, or your written quote, plus applicable taxes. Late or unpaid
amounts may accrue interest at the maximum rate permitted by law, plus
reasonable costs of collection, including attorneys' fees where allowed.

We reserve the right to collect amounts lawfully owed using any lawful
means, which may include: charging the payment method on file, suspending
or terminating accounts, seats, workspaces, or self-host keys, offsetting
against coin credits otherwise due (coins are never payable in cash), engaging a collection agency or
counsel, and pursuing claims in court. Prepaying minimizes interruptions
and collection action. Nothing here limits defenses or rights available
to you under applicable law.

Self-hosted subscriptions renew monthly until cancelled per the Terms or
your order. Cancelling stops future renewals; it does not refund
completed periods and does not retroactively license past unlicensed use.

